README
======

BicycleRoad — a JOSM plugin

Author:  Till Butenschön <Till.Butenschoen@student.hpi.de>
License: GPL v2 or later (see the LICENSE file)

Purpose
-------
Speeds up tagging ways as a bicycle road ("Fahrradstraße") or bicycle zone
("Fahrradzone"), optionally adding one or more supplementary signs
("Zusatzzeichen").

It adds a "Tag bicycle road" command to the Data menu (and, optionally, the
toolbar). Triggering it opens a dialog where you pick:

  1. the road type        — Fahrradstraße / Fahrradzone (exactly one)
  2. additional signs      — any number, via checkboxes:
       Anlieger frei, KFZ frei, Landwirtschaftlicher Verkehr frei,
       Forstwirtschaftlicher Verkehr frei,
       Land- und Forstwirtschaftlicher Verkehr frei, Linienverkehr frei

Each option shows its real traffic-sign image; the currently selected ones are
marked with a coloured border. Some signs are mutually exclusive (e.g. "Anlieger
frei" and "KFZ frei"): selecting one automatically deselects the other.

The last choice is remembered (in the JOSM preferences) and pre-selected the
next time, and the OK/Apply button is the default. So the common workflow

    select way(s)  ->  trigger action  ->  press Enter

re-applies the previous combination to everything selected in one undoable
step.

Tags
----
The OSM key/value pairs written for each option live in one place:

    src/org/openstreetmap/josm/plugins/bicycleroad/BicycleRoadTags.java

Base tags by type:

  Fahrradstraße            Fahrradzone
  bicycle=designated       bicycle=designated
  bicycle_road=yes         bicycle_road=yes
  traffic_sign=DE:244.1    traffic_sign=DE:244.3
  maxspeed=30              maxspeed=30
  source:maxspeed=         source:maxspeed=
    DE:bicycle_road          DE:bicycle_zone
  vehicle=no               vehicle=no

Additional signs then modify the base. Each appends its code to traffic_sign
(comma-separated) and contributes override tags:

  Anlieger frei                  +1020-30   vehicle=destination
  KFZ frei                       +KFZ frei  motor_vehicle=yes,
                                            traffic_sign:note="Zusatzzeichen:
                                            kombiniertes Schild aus 1024-10,
                                            1022-12 ohne eigene Nummer"
  Landwirtschaftl. Verkehr frei  +1026-36   vehicle=agricultural
  Forstwirtschaftl. Verkehr frei +1026-37   vehicle=forestry
  Land- u. Forstwirtsch. frei    +1026-38   vehicle=agricultural;forestry
  Linienverkehr frei             +1026-32   bus=yes

When several signs are selected, their traffic_sign codes are appended in order
and override values for the same key are merged with ";". Example —
Fahrradstraße + Anlieger frei + Forstwirtschaftlicher Verkehr frei:

  traffic_sign=DE:244.1,1020-30,1026-37
  vehicle=destination;forestry

Combination rule (see inConflict() in BicycleRoadTags.java): only "Anlieger
frei" may be combined with another sign — and not with "KFZ frei". Every other
pair is mutually exclusive (selecting one deselects the conflicting one), since
e.g. "KFZ frei" + "Linienverkehr frei" or two overlapping agricultural/forestry
signs make no sense together.

Re-applying replaces a previous tagging cleanly: optional keys a sign sets
(motor_vehicle, bus, traffic_sign:note) are removed again when no currently
selected sign sets them, so switching from "KFZ frei" to something else does
not leave a stale motor_vehicle=yes behind.

To change any of these, edit BicycleRoadTags.java — the dialog and apply logic
need no changes.

Keyboard shortcut
-----------------
The action registers a shortcut entry but binds no key by default (to avoid
clashing with JOSM core or other plugins). Assign one under
Preferences > Keyboard Shortcuts — search for "bicycle road".

Building
--------
Maven (uses the JOSM core artifact from your local ~/.m2):

    mvn -pl bicycleroad package

The plugin jar is written to target/bicycleroad.jar. Install it by copying it
into your JOSM plugins directory, or use `ant install` (see build.xml).
